THE SIX PATHS (all under infra/aws/ec2/opal-gateway/): app/harvest_research.py M, app/harvest_figures.py M, app/harvest_identity.py M, app/harvest_keys.py M, tests/test_cj6_slash_key_other_tools.py M, tests/test_ck2_path_component_union_read.py A. git diff --name-status live..release lists exactly these six (5 M, 1 A; 573 insertions, 30 deletions). Each carried file's md5 equals the pair's table; the five modified files at the live commit equal the pair's last column (the equality guard). 82 tests passed on the release branch (test_og_gt8 red before and after, not a gate). The bun cache precheck reads 77 of 77.
WHAT CHANGES FOR THE HOST: the opal-gateway service restarts once (about a minute, every MCP tool for every principal on every box). Served moves only for BP/_LN_Equity and NG/_LN_Equity on the path-component tools (peers and scores, coverage, filing analysis, fundamentals, management roster): the union of the canonical and the legacy raw prefix, the canonical object winning a same-name collision, a stored_spelling map on the response. Keys without a slash are byte-equal. No S3 object, IAM, Terraform or schedule change. tools.py and server.py are not touched.
INTENDED WINDOW (UTC): start at the issuer's GO, no earlier than 13:58Z; end by 15:00Z, inside site Z's CLEAR to about 15:10Z (its msg 35704). The deploy itself is about three minutes (build, upload, restart, health). Site Z's round 43 is a trunk merge only, no host act; an in-flight release on the host in the window is a STOP.
